= Differential Geometry and General Relativity

== Christoffel Symbols and Metric Compatibility

Let $(cal(M), g)$ be a pseudo-Riemannian manifold of dimension $n$ equipped with metric tensor $g_(mu nu)$. The Levi-Civita connection satisfies metric compatibility $nabla_lambda g_(mu nu) = 0$ and torsion-freeness $Gamma^lambda_(mu nu) = Gamma^lambda_(nu mu)$. The Christoffel symbols of the second kind are given explicitly by:

$ Gamma^lambda_(mu nu) = 1 / 2 g^(lambda sigma) (partial_mu g_(nu sigma) + partial_nu g_(mu sigma) - partial_sigma g_(mu nu)) $ <eq-christoffel>

The covariant derivative of a mixed tensor field $T^mu_nu$ along vector field $X^alpha$ takes the form:

$ nabla_alpha T^mu_nu = partial_alpha T^mu_nu + Gamma^mu_(alpha sigma) T^sigma_nu - Gamma^sigma_(alpha nu) T^mu_sigma $

== Curvature Tensors and Field Equations

The Riemann curvature tensor measures the failure of covariant derivatives to commute:

$ [nabla_mu, nabla_nu] V^lambda = R^lambda_(sigma mu nu) V^sigma $

In local coordinate charts, the components of the Riemann tensor are expressed as:

$ R^rho_(sigma mu nu) = partial_mu Gamma^rho_(nu sigma) - partial_nu Gamma^rho_(mu sigma) + Gamma^rho_(mu lambda) Gamma^lambda_(nu sigma) - Gamma^rho_(nu lambda) Gamma^lambda_(mu sigma) $

Contracting the first and third indices yields the symmetric Ricci tensor $R_(mu nu) = R^lambda_(mu lambda nu)$, whose contraction with the inverse metric gives the Ricci scalar curvature:

$ R = g^(mu nu) R_(mu nu) = g^(mu nu) (partial_lambda Gamma^lambda_(nu mu) - partial_nu Gamma^lambda_(lambda mu) + Gamma^lambda_(lambda sigma) Gamma^sigma_(nu mu) - Gamma^lambda_(nu sigma) Gamma^sigma_(lambda mu)) $

The Einstein field equations with non-zero cosmological constant $Lambda$ couple geometry to the stress-energy tensor $T_(mu nu)$:

$ R_(mu nu) - 1 / 2 R g_(mu nu) + Lambda g_(mu nu) = (8 pi G) / c^4 T_(mu nu) $

The contracted Bianchi identities $nabla^mu (R_(mu nu) - 1/2 R g_(mu nu)) = 0$ ensure local conservation of energy-momentum $nabla^mu T_(mu nu) = 0$.

